<title>HONG KONG: HK to tender HK$500 mln in two-year notes May 12.</title>
<headline>HK to tender HK$500 mln in two-year notes May 12.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hong Kong Monetary Authority said it would tender HK$500 million in two-year notes on May 12 to settle on May 13.</p>
<p>An additional HK$100 million will be held as a reserve for supply to market makers in the secondary market, the HKMA said.</p>
<p>The notes will mature on May 13 and carry an interest rate of 6.12 percent, payable semi-annually in arrears.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
